From ace845b16c2b40ad8728dfb7f94160ca3ec644f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:47:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Record the freshness policy decision and pin its boundaries
 (#47)

Team 1 decision: keep the implemented limits as an approved deviation from
the handoff (observations 5 min old / 60 s ahead; NWS issuance 6 h old /
5 min ahead; per-city cache retrieval 6 h).

- frontend/freshness-policy.js is the single source; contract.js,
  weather.js, engine/evaluate.js and app.js read from it. The displayed-
  model expiry in app.js used its own copy of 6 h / 5 min and now calls
  validateForecastIssuance. Values and behaviour are unchanged.
- assertFresh rejects missing or invalid timestamps instead of letting
  NaN pass; visible messages state the limit.
- docs/FRESHNESS_POLICY.md: limits, rationale, the four separate times,
  where each limit applies, and the three PR #37 spec cases that
  intentionally differ (SPEC-FORECAST-AGE 7201 s and -7 s,
  SPEC-FRESHNESS -6 s) with the boundaries they should move to.
- tests/freshness-policy.test.mjs: exact boundaries, stale issuance with
  future-valid periods, cached rechecks and coverage, missing/invalid
  timestamps, city isolation, deterministic clocks.
- e2e: a displayed model survives a failed refresh only until its issuance
  passes 6 hours.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
